  "summary_en": "CORDIS news article on an EU-funded study (SAFEandSOUND, EUROBENCH) assessing ISO 13482:2014 for lower-limb robotic exoskeletons. It finds the standard leaves gaps on safety, ethical and social issues, and recommends type-specific standards and shared stakeholder responsibility.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "ISO 13482:2014 does not address safety sufficiently or comprehensively for wearable robots.",
   "Scope, risk definition, and psychological and gender aspects of safety need improvement.",
   "Covering diverse robot types in one standard creates confusion about required safeguards.",
   "Separate standards per robot type (e.g., physical assistant vs social robots) are suggested.",
   "All stakeholders must share responsibility for safety and functionality."
